    examples: [{ title: 'Average sleep of 62 mammals', origin: 'pdf', ref: 'p. 1', problem: 'Find the mean of dat$TotalSleep, which has 4 missing values.', solution: [{ text: 'mean(dat$TotalSleep) gives [1] NA: one unknown makes the mean unknown.' }, { text: 'mean(dat$TotalSleep, na.rm = TRUE) drops the 4 NAs and averages the remaining 58 values.' }], answer: '10.53276 hours per day.' }],
    code: code([['mean(dat$TotalSleep)', 'na.rm is left at its default FALSE, so the NAs stay in and the result is NA.'], ['mean(dat$TotalSleep, na.rm = TRUE)', 'the named argument removes the NAs before averaging.']], ['[1] NA', '[1] 10.53276'], 'NA is not an error: it tells you the data have gaps that you must decide how to treat.'),
    terms: [{ term: 'NA', meaning: '"not available": R\'s marker for a missing value' }, { term: 'na.rm', meaning: 'argument of mean(), sd(), sum() …: TRUE removes NAs before computing; default FALSE' }],
